title: where we differ
pid: d65e59f0-b6e2-4632-b68f-9ec3611d6f35
body: |2-
  His sketch begins from a subscription. I had none: his week of changes was spread over music, the team, skg, puzzles and his mailboxes. A reader needs first a view of everything one author changed, and only then the subscriptions.
  His "pruned change view" takes its starting point from his commits (his HEAD, or HEAD-1). Most of his week was uncommitted, and one commit called "more" holds days of work. What a reader needs is the point where they themselves last marked a note read, which his "mark processed" note already keeps. I would let those marks define where the pruned view begins.
  The live notice from the reader's log is not in his sketch, and it was the one thing that worked.
  He imagines reading depth first. Skg gave me no tree of changes to walk at all, so I read in the order Git listed files.
